---
// /community - near-verbatim port of community-8-25 (Jon: "I like almost everything
// about this page"). ONLY the offer/pricing model changes (community-page-spec.md):
// Pricing model (Jon, 2026-08-21): ONE option - a single $291 payment covering
// 3 months, i.e. $97/month paid up front. NOT a subscription. It simply ends;
// members who want to stay opt in to $37/mo afterwards and Jon sends that link
// by hand.
//   - $291 = 3 x $97 ON PURPOSE. It preserves the homepage device ("Either way,
//     you start for $97") where the community and the 1:1 session share an
//     entry price. Do not change one without the other.
//   - Always pair "$97/month" with "paid up front". Jon: "I don't want it to
//     look like they can sub by the month."
//   - Do NOT say the membership "automatically continues" - nothing renews.
//     Stripe has no record of the 3-month term; a one-time payment has no
//     duration. Jon tracks end dates himself.
//   - NO strikethrough pricing, ever. $291 is the price. Specials are Stripe
//     coupon codes applied at checkout, never a crossed-out number on the page.
//     There is no cheaper community tier - the low-cost door is the $97 1:1
//     session (Jon, 2026-08-21).
// The old "$97/mo x3 or $250 one-pay (save $41)" pair is GONE, along with the
// $147-regular and discount-code apparatus.
// Rationale wording is deliberate: "quitting is a process that takes time" -
// NEVER "that's how long transformation takes", which is a timeline promise and
// violates PRD rule 3. Jon rejected that phrasing explicitly.
// Design: varied treatments per critique - split rows w/ icons, numbered journey,
// ticket pricing. No back-to-back card grids.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';

// Community video - self-hosted, NOT YouTube (Jon, 2026-08-14).
// Encoded from the 732MB / 15.1 Mbps master down to 44MB / 954 kbps.
// TODO (PRD #15): move these files to Cloudflare R2 and update the paths.

// Checkout for the $291 / 3-month membership. Stripe collects the money; Jon
// then invites them into Mighty Networks BY HAND. Mighty is no longer the
// checkout - the old mn.co/plans/1948481 link sold the retired $97/mo plan.
//
// 🚨 CURRENTLY A SANDBOX TEST LINK ("test_" in the URL). It cannot take real
// money. SWAP FOR THE LIVE PAYMENT LINK BEFORE LAUNCH - see SETUP.md
// "Going live". The build warns if a test link is still wired up.
const JOIN_URL = 'https://buy.stripe.com/test_aFafZaf6RehnbXo2Yt2oE02';

if (JOIN_URL.includes('/test_')) {
  console.warn(
    '\n⚠️  /community is using a STRIPE SANDBOX link (test_...). ' +
      'It cannot accept real payments. Replace JOIN_URL before launch.\n'
  );
}
---

<Base
  title="Join the AlwaysBeQuitting Community"
  description="Weekly expert coaching and ongoing community support for your quit smoking or vaping journey. $291 for 3 months - $97/month, paid up front."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <!-- hero: video + pricing ticket -->
  <header class="band band--teal" style="padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem)">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="display-xl" style="text-align:center; color:var(--white)">Join the AlwaysBeQuitting Community</h1>
      <p style="text-align:center; font-size:1.2rem; margin:1.2rem auto 2.6rem; max-width:46rem; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 85%, transparent)">
        Weekly Expert Coaching + Ongoing Community Support For Your Entire Quit Smoking or Vaping Journey
      </p>
      <div class="hero-split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <VideoEmbed
            src720="/video/community-720p.mp4"
            src480="/video/community-480p.mp4"
            poster="/video/community-poster.webp"
            posterMobile="/video/community-poster-480.webp"
            posterFallback="/video/community-poster.jpg"
            title="Jon introduces the AlwaysBeQuitting community"
          />
        </div>
        <aside class="ticket reveal">
          <p class="ticket__kicker">Full ABQ Community Membership</p>
          <p class="ticket__price">$291<span>3 months at $97/month, paid up front</span></p>
          <p class="ticket__terms">Three months is a commitment to yourself and to the process of quitting, which takes time.</p>
          <p class="ticket__then">After that, you can continue at <strong>$37/month</strong> if you wish.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--cta" href={JOIN_URL}>Join the Community</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- what you get: each feature is its own full-width alternating band -->
  <section class="band band--white" style="padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-lg" style="text-align:center">What You Get</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--white feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split reveal">
        <div class="row-split__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="4" y="10" width="28" height="24" rx="4"></rect>
            <path d="M32 20l12-7v22l-12-7"></path>
            <circle cx="18" cy="20" r="4"></circle>
            <path d="M11 30c1.5-3 4-4.5 7-4.5s5.5 1.5 7 4.5"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Weekly Community Support Calls</h3>
          <p>
            Join Jon for live group coaching - usually one call a week, sometimes more. Ask questions, get guidance
            on whatever you're dealing with that week, and hear from others on the same journey.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Can't make it live?</strong> All calls are recorded and accessible in the community.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--alt feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split row-split--flip reveal">
        <div class="row-split__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M8 8h24a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v12a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H20l-8 7v-7H8a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V12a4 4 0 0 1 4-4z"></path>
            <path d="M40 18h.5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v10a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H38v6l-7-6h-7"></path>
            <path d="M12 16h16M12 22h10"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>24/7 Community Access</h3>
          <p>
            Connect with others who understand what you're going through. Share wins, get support during struggles,
            and <strong>never feel alone in your quitting journey.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--white feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split reveal">
        <div class="row-split__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M10 44V6"></path>
            <path d="M10 8h26l-6 8 6 8H10"></path>
            <path d="M6 44h8"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Real Accountability Throughout Your Journey</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Stay motivated and accelerate your commitment to quit.</strong> Post your progress, share
            challenges, get encouragement when you need it most. Jon is active in the community providing guidance
            between calls.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--alt feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split row-split--flip reveal">
        <div class="row-split__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="20"></circle>
            <path d="M31 17l-4.5 9.5L17 31l4.5-9.5z"></path>
            <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="1.6" fill="currentColor"></circle>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Build Your Own Plan - Quit at Your Pace</h3>
          <p>You don't follow a one-size-fits-all program (they rarely work). And you don't figure it out alone.</p>
          <p>
            <strong>You create YOUR plan</strong> - when to start, what pace works for your life, whether you take
            big steps, baby steps, or both. <strong>Jon guides you through it</strong> - helping you shape a plan
            that actually works, avoiding the common pitfalls, and supporting you through the countless ways you
            can get derailed.
          </p>
          <p>
            There are millions of ways to fail at quitting. <strong>There are proven ways to succeed.</strong> Our
            unique quitting community can help you find your path through it all.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- four stages: numbered journey -->
  <section class="band band--mist" style="padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6.5rem)">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:880px">
      <!-- Q and A are a matched pair at the SAME size, as on the live site
           (Jon, 2026-08-14). The Q was previously .kicker - tiny tracked-out
           label type - which buried the teaser under its own answer. -->
      <p class="display-lg" style="text-align:center; font-style:italic; margin:0">
        Q: How do I know if the ABQ community is right for me?
      </p>
      <h2 class="display-lg" style="text-align:center; margin-top:1.4rem">
        A: Which of these best describes where you are with your smoking or vaping?
      </h2>
      <div class="options">
        <div class="option reveal">
          <span class="option__badge">A</span>
          <h3>You want to quit someday, you just keep putting it off.</h3>
          <p>You feel stuck (like 99.9% of the smokers and vapers on the planet). You're scared to even try to quit. But you have this nagging feeling inside.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>That's okay.</strong> Join now. Use the community and weekly calls to build your confidence and readiness. There's no pressure to quit on day one. Just show up. You'll move forward.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option reveal">
          <span class="option__badge">B</span>
          <h3>You're finally "ready to quit" and want to set a quit date</h3>
          <p>You've decided - this is it. You want support through the first days, weeks, and months. You may have no idea how to proceed, or you may be crafting a plan.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>Perfect.</strong> You're in charge and we can help get some quitting time under your belt. The community gives you accountability and expert guidance exactly when you need it most.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option reveal">
          <span class="option__badge">C</span>
          <h3>You've already quit but want to make sure it lasts this time</h3>
          <p>You stopped smoking or vaping, but you're worried about going back. You need accountability to stay quit.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>You're in the right place.</strong> The transformation from temporary abstinence to permanent non-smoker / non-vaper is where most people need the most support. Real transformation takes months. We will be here for you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option reveal">
          <span class="option__badge">D</span>
          <h3>You relapsed and want to get back on track</h3>
          <p>You had some smoke-free or vape-free time, but you went back to it. You are on the "quit-relapse" treadmill and you want to get off it.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>Don't let shame keep you out.</strong> This is exactly why ongoing support matters. Come back, get motivation from being in the community, fix the things that tripped you up, and start moving forward again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align:center; margin-top:2rem; font-size:1.1rem"><strong>Whichever you picked - the answer is the same. This community was built for exactly where you are.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- simple truth band -->
  <section class="band band--teal transform">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <h2 class="display-lg" style="margin-top:1rem">
        If you're struggling to quit smoking or vaping on your own, joining the ABQ community is the right decision.
      </h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- pricing: ticket, full detail [DIFF: new model, codes removed] -->
  <section class="band band--white" style="padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6.5rem)">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">
      <div class="ticket ticket--big reveal">
        <p class="ticket__kicker">Full ABQ Community Membership</p>
        <p class="ticket__price">$291<span>3 months at $97/month, paid up front</span></p>
        <p class="ticket__terms">
          Three months is a commitment to yourself and to the process of quitting, which takes time.
        </p>
        <p class="ticket__then">
          After your 3 months, you can continue at <strong>$37/month if you wish</strong> - for as long as you
          want. The longer you stay, the cheaper it gets - the opposite of every program that's burned you.
        </p>
        <p class="ticket__alt">
          Your commitment to transformation is 3 months. After that, it's up to you whether you continue.
          No refunds on the $291.
        </p>
        <ul class="checks checks--ink">
          <li>24/7 access to community support</li>
          <li>Community Support Calls - usually one a week, schedule published at the start of each month</li>
          <li>Access to call recordings + ability to ask questions beforehand</li>
          <li>Accountability check-ins (voluntary and without shock collars 🙂)</li>
          <li>Expert guidance on withdrawal, mindset, and behavior change</li>
          <li>Quit at your pace - no rigid timeline to follow</li>
          <li>Positive, committed community (no lurkers or trial members)</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn btn--cta" href={JOIN_URL} style="align-self:center">Join the Community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- just start / antidote close -->
  <section class="band band--paper" style="padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem); text-align:center">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">
      <h2 class="display-lg">Just Start.</h2>
      <p style="font-size:1.15rem; margin-top:1.4rem; color:var(--soft)">
        The ABQ community is an insane value. Most people spend hundreds a month on smoking or vaping -
        <strong style="color:var(--ink)">you'll save hundreds of thousands over your lifetime by quitting.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="display-lg hl reveal" style="margin-top:2rem; font-size:clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem)">
        You're already spending the money. You're just giving it to companies that make you sick. We don't compare
        ourselves to those companies; <em>we are the antidote to those companies.</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- testimonials -->
  <section class="band band--white proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>It took me nearly six years to build the courage to find a specialist and I am unbelievably grateful it was Jon. If you have reservations about investing in a coach, I cannot recommend Jon enough. The impact he has had on my life is transformative.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Katherine</b> · One Year Vape Free</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>Jon's non-assuming approach and meeting me where I was at was really helpful. Having the support and the accountability - it's kind of two sides of the same coin. That was probably one of the pieces that I was missing.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Kait</b> · 9 Years Sober, Now Smoke-Free</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>I've invited Jon to teach about tobacco treatment to my "Health Counseling" university class for 9 straight semesters. His presentations are informative, entertaining and inspiring.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Ashley Foster</b> · MPH, RD, CHES · University Professor</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ - verbatim except subscription item [DIFF] -->
  <section class="band band--mist">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <h2 class="display-lg">Common Questions</h2>
      <!-- VERBATIM from the live site (Jon, 2026-08-14). A previous rewrite
           flattened both bulleted lists into run-on sentences and dropped the
           judgment-free line and the consulting/training note. Keep the lists. -->
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>Who can join ABQ programs and community?</summary>
        <p>
          This community is for people who smoke or vape and want to quit - or who recently quit and need support
          to stay quit.
        </p>
        <p><strong>You're welcome to join if you are:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Currently use tobacco, nicotine, or vaping products and want to quit</li>
          <li>Recently quit but are struggling to maintain it</li>
          <li>Relapsed and need support to get back on track</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>To maintain a focused, supportive environment, we don't allow:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Healthcare professionals (unless you're personally seeking help for your own tobacco/nicotine use, and inform us of it)</li>
          <li>Anyone affiliated with the tobacco, nicotine, or vaping industry</li>
          <li>People looking to learn our methods for their own coaching, training, or business purposes</li>
          <li>Anyone misrepresenting their tobacco/nicotine use status</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Why?</strong> Our community thrives when everyone is genuinely focused on their own quitting
          journey. This creates the judgment-free environment that helps people succeed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Violating these requirements results in immediate removal with no refund, as outlined in our complete
          <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Note:</strong> If you're interested in our training methods for professional purposes, we offer
          separate consulting and training services. Feel free to contact us directly to discuss those options.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>When do the Community Support Calls happen? What if I miss one?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>Current Schedule:</strong> Community Support Calls are scheduled at the beginning of the month.
          There is usually one per week, sometimes more.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Please note:</strong> We try to choose different times of the day so that both US and
          international members have a chance to attend. We publish the schedule at the beginning of each month.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Can't make it live?</strong> All calls are recorded and available to watch later. You can also
          submit questions ahead of time, and Jon will answer them during the call even if you can't attend live.
        </p>
        <p>
          Plus, you have 24/7 access to the community where you can get support, ask questions, and connect with
          others any time.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>How long should I stay in the community?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>The short answer:</strong> as long as you need. <strong>The realistic answer:</strong> real
          transformation typically takes 3–6 months, especially for longer-term smokers and vapers - that's exactly
          why membership starts with a 3-month commitment. Let's face it: things are going to come up. If you want
          the best shot at quitting for life, don't focus on quitting the community.
          <strong>FOCUS ON QUITTING smoking or vaping for life. That is the end game.</strong> After your first
          3 months, you can continue at just $37/month if you wish - and how long you stay is entirely up to you.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>What's your subscription, cancellation, and refund policy?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>Your membership:</strong> ABQ Community membership is one payment of $291 - $97/month for 3 months,
          paid up front. All 3 months are yours and the payment stands; we
          don't offer refunds for any reason. This isn't because we don't stand behind what we do - it's because
          transformation requires commitment, and an "easy out" encourages giving up exactly when things get
          challenging. <strong>After 3 months:</strong> your membership ends unless you choose to continue. If you
          want to stay, it's $37/month for as long as you like - just let me know and I'll send you the link.
          <strong>What we guarantee:</strong> the
          delivery of weekly Community Support Calls, ongoing community access, and Jon's guidance.
          <strong>What we can't guarantee:</strong> that you'll quit. Your success depends on factors under your
          control - your mindset, decisions, commitment, and how you navigate the challenges. We provide guidance,
          accountability, and support, but we can't execute the process for you. We think you can do this!
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>Is this community confidential?</summary>
        <p><strong>No, this community is NOT confidential like a doctor's office or therapist's office.</strong></p>
        <p>Here's what that means:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Other members will see what you post in the community</li>
          <li>Other members will hear what you say on Community Support Calls</li>
          <li>We can't control what others remember or discuss outside the community</li>
          <li>This is peer support and coaching - not medical or therapeutic care with confidentiality protections</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Only share what you're comfortable with others knowing.</strong></p>
        <p>
          If you need medical care or therapy with full confidentiality protections, please seek those services
          from licensed healthcare professionals.
        </p>
        <p>
          For complete medical disclaimers, liability limitations, and additional legal protections, please see our
          full <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
      <!-- MEDICAL DISCLAIMER - VERBATIM from the live site (Jon, 2026-08-14).
           Restored in full after a condensed rewrite dropped roughly two-thirds
           of it, including the entire "Medication Discussions" and "Our
           Commitment to You" sections. DO NOT edit, shorten, or "tidy" this
           text. Legal/medical wording is never changed on a judgment call. -->
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>Medical Disclaimer</summary>
        <p>
          We know this isn't the most exciting thing to read, but we need to be crystal clear about what we offer
          and what we don't.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What We Provide</strong><br />
          All of our services—coaching, community support, and educational materials—are for information and
          education only. We're here to provide guidance, support, accountability, and proven strategies to help
          you on your quitting journey.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What We Don't Provide</strong><br />
          Our services are NOT medical, mental health, or addiction treatment. We are not doctors, therapists, or
          medical professionals. Our coaching and community do not constitute medical care. While we're passionate
          about helping you quit and have extensive experience in this area, we cannot replace professional
          healthcare.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Your Responsibility</strong><br />
          It's your responsibility to verify with your doctor, healthcare provider, or therapist that our
          information and guidance are appropriate for your specific situation. You assume all responsibility for
          how you apply what you learn in our programs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>When to Seek Medical Care</strong><br />
          If you're experiencing thoughts of self-harm, severe depression, serious physical symptoms, or any mental
          health crisis, please seek immediate professional medical attention. Call 911 in any emergency situation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Medication Discussions</strong><br />
          We may discuss various cessation aids, medications, and products as educational information only. Any
          medication decisions must be made in consultation with qualified healthcare professionals. We are not
          prescribing or personally recommending specific medications for your individual use.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Our Commitment to You</strong><br />
          While we can't provide medical treatment, we are absolutely committed to providing you with the best
          educational resources, coaching support, and community encouragement to help you succeed in your quitting
          journey. We believe in your ability to quit, and we're here to support you every step of the way!
        </p>
        <p>
          If you want medical care or mental health treatment, we encourage you to pursue that with professional
          treatment facilities and providers.
        </p>
        <p>
          For complete medical disclaimers, liability limitations, and additional legal protections, please see our
          full <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- final cta -->
  <section class="band band--teal final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-xl hl">Finally become the non-smoker or non-vaper <em>you dreamed about.</em></h2>
      <p style="margin-top:1.4rem; font-size:1.15rem; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 85%, transparent)">
        Imagine waking up breathing freely. Not thinking about when you can smoke or vape next. Not hiding it or
        making excuses. Not spending hundreds every month on something that's hurting you.
        <strong style="color:var(--white)">That's what transformation looks like. You can do this.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="final__actions reveal">
        <a class="btn btn--cta" href={JOIN_URL}>Join the Community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-split {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero-split {
      grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr;
    }
  }
  .video {
    aspect-ratio: 16/9;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--alt), var(--alt) 10px, var(--white) 10px, var(--white) 20px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--soft);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: 12px 12px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 22%, transparent);
  }
  .ticket {
    background: var(--white);
    color: var(--ink);
